# Vendor and Store Rules

- Vendor and Store are separate bounded contexts under `backend/src/modules/`.
- Store always belongs to exactly one vendor; validate ownership on every mutation.
- Never trust `vendorId` or `storeId` from request bodies without matching authenticated scope.
- Vendor lifecycle: `PENDING -> UNDER_REVIEW -> APPROVED -> ACTIVE -> SUSPENDED`.
- Store lifecycle: `DRAFT -> ACTIVE -> SUSPENDED -> CLOSED`.
- Store offers bind catalog products to store-specific price/availability; do not duplicate catalog identity inside offers.
- Cross-module catalog access uses Catalog application ports only.
- Emit lifecycle events through the transactional outbox for downstream indexing and notifications.
- Admin-only actions (vendor approval, platform suspension) require explicit platform permissions and audit logging.
